><nav class="wz-modal__tabs" role="tablist" aria-label="StratOps introduction sections"><button class="wz-modal__tab is-active" type="button" data-tab="intro" id="wz-intro-tab-intro" role="tab" aria-selected="true" aria-controls="wz-intro-content-view" tabindex="0">Overview</button> <button class="wz-modal__tab" type="button" data-tab="capabilities" id="wz-intro-tab-capabilities" role="tab" aria-selected="false" aria-controls="wz-intro-capabilities" tabindex="-1">Operational Capabilities</button> <button class="wz-modal__tab" type="button" data-tab="terms" id="wz-intro-tab-terms" role="tab" aria-selected="false" aria-controls="wz-intro-terms" tabindex="-1">Rules of Engagement</button></nav><section class="wz-modal-body"><div id="wz-intro-content-view" class="wz-content is-active" data-pane="intro" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="wz-intro-tab-intro" aria-hidden="false"><h2 id="wz-intro-title">Real-Time Multi-Domain Battlespace Intelligence</h2><p id="wz-intro-summary"><strong>StratOps</strong>, powered by <strong><a href="https://battlespacex.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">BattlespaceX</a></strong>, is a real-time, multi-domain intelligence visualization platform that leverages OSINT to synthesize aggregated telemetry streams and event signals into a live, 3D layered battlespace spanning air, land, sea, space, and cyberspace. It supports tracking of military movements, assessment of escalation dynamics, and continuous interpretation of operational changes within a theater of operations, in near real time.</p></div><div id="wz-intro-login-view" class="wz-content" aria-hidden="true"><h2 id="wz-login-title">Sign In to StratOps</h2><p>Log in with your <strong>BattlespaceX</strong> account to unlock full capabilities.</p><p id="intro-auth-error" class="wz-error-container" hidden aria-live="assertive" role="alert"></p><form id="intro-auth-form" novalidate aria-labelledby="intro-auth-form-label"><span id="intro-auth-form-label" class="sr-only">Intro login form</span><div class="wz-form-container" role="group" aria-labelledby="intro-auth-fields-label"><span id="intro-auth-fields-label" class="sr-only">Login credentials</span><div class="wz-form-fieldbox"><label for="intro-auth-email">E-mail</label> <input id="intro-auth-email" type="email" autocomplete="username" inputmode="email" class="wz--input" required aria-required="true" aria-describedby="intro-email-help"/> <span id="intro-email-help" class="sr-only">Enter your registered email address</span></div><div class="wz-form-fieldbox"><label for="intro-auth-password">Password</label> <input id="intro-auth-password" type="password" autocomplete="current-password" class="wz--input" required aria-required="true" aria-describedby="intro-password-help"/> <span id="intro-password-help" class="sr-only">Enter your account password</span></div></div><div class="wz-check" for="intro-auth-remember"><input id="intro-auth-remember" type="checkbox"/> <span>Stay connected</span></div></form><div class="wz-footer" role="group" aria-label="Account creation option"><span>New to StratOps?</span> <button class="btn-secondary purple" type="button" onclick="window.location.href='https://www.battlespacex.com/register?returnUrl=https://stratops.battlespacex.com'" aria-label="Create a BattlespaceX account to access StratOps"><span aria-hidden="true"></span> <i class="static-icon stratops-ico-assets-recon-intel-1" aria-hidden="true"></i> Create Account</button></div></div><div id="wz-intro-capabilities" class="wz-content" data-pane="capabilities" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="wz-intro-tab-capabilities" aria-hidden="true"><h3 class="no-margin">Advanced Operational Capabilities</h3><ul class="wz-list-view"><li>Multi-domain battlespace visualization spanning air, land, sea, space, and cyberspace.</li><li>3D military aircraft and naval vessel models support immersive asset tracking and close-range operational visualization.</li><li>Continuous monitoring of military activity, operational events, escalation indicators, strategic developments, and emerging global flashpoints.</li><li>Integrated intelligence layers combining OSINT, telemetry, military infrastructure, geospatial context, and operational activity.</li><li>Region and Conflict Lens controls enable focused analysis of active conflicts, strategic theaters, standoffs, and global activity.</li><li>Premium operational overlays including radar coverage, threat rings, engagement ranges, and area-of-influence visualization.</li></ul><p><strong>StratOps</strong> aims to become a next-generation OSINT visualization environment for research, media awareness, analytical observation, and strategic monitoring of global security developments.</p></div><div id="wz-intro-terms" class="wz-content" data-pane="terms" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="wz-intro-tab-terms" aria-hidden="true"><h3 class="no-margin">Acceptance of These Rules</h3><p>By accessing, viewing, or using StratOps, you acknowledge and agree to these Rules of Engagement and Terms of Use.</p><p>If you do not agree with these terms, you must discontinue use of the platform.</p><h3>Information Sources</h3><p>StratOps relies on publicly available information, including but not limited to:</p><ul class="wz-list-view"><li>Open-source intelligence (OSINT)</li><li>Public aviation and maritime data</li><li>Government publications</li><li>News and media reporting</li><li>Publicly accessible telemetry and event feeds</li><li>Publicly available satellite and geospatial information</li><li>User-submitted and community-sourced observations where applicable</li></ul><p>Information displayed on the platform may be incomplete, delayed, inaccurate, misreported, disputed, or subsequently corrected.</p><p>Users are responsible for independently verifying any information before relying upon it.</p><h3>No Operational Authority</h3><p>StratOps does not issue:</p><ul class="wz-list-view"><li>Military orders</li><li>Security instructions</li><li>Emergency directives</li><li>Airspace advisories</li><li>Maritime navigation instructions</li><li>Evacuation notices</li><li>Civil defense guidance</li><li>Official threat warnings</li></ul><p>Nothing displayed on StratOps should be interpreted as official direction from any government, military, intelligence organization, emergency management agency, aviation authority, maritime authority, or public institution.</p><h3>Accuracy &amp; Reliability Disclaimer</h3><p>While reasonable efforts are made to maintain data quality and operational readability, StratOps makes no representation or warranty regarding:</p><ul class="wz-list-view"><li>Accuracy</li><li>Completeness</li><li>Reliability</li><li>Timeliness</li><li>Availability</li><li>Operational relevance</li></ul><p>Displayed tracks, events, alerts, incidents, classifications, visualizations, locations, movements, assessments, and indicators may contain errors or omissions.</p><p>Users assume full responsibility for any interpretation or use of information presented through the platform.</p><h3>Intelligence Classification Disclaimer</h3><p>All information presented within StratOps is derived from publicly accessible sources unless explicitly stated otherwise.</p><p>StratOps does not claim access to classified, restricted, protected, confidential, or government-controlled intelligence.</p><p>Visualizations, assessments, indicators, alerts, and classifications generated by the platform represent informational interpretations of open-source information and should not be considered authoritative intelligence products.</p><h3>Permitted Use</h3><p>Users may access and utilize StratOps for:</p><ul class="wz-list-view"><li>Research</li><li>Education</li><li>Journalism</li><li>Situational awareness</li><li>Academic work</li><li>Public-interest analysis</li><li>Security and geopolitical observation</li><li>Non-commercial review and evaluation</li></ul><p>All use must comply with applicable laws and regulations.</p><h3>Prohibited Activities</h3><p>Users may not:</p><ul class="wz-list-view"><li>Attempt unauthorized access to systems or infrastructure</li><li>Interfere with platform operations</li><li>Reverse engineer proprietary platform functionality</li><li>Circumvent security mechanisms</li><li>Use the platform to facilitate unlawful activity</li><li>Misrepresent StratOps content as official intelligence</li><li>Falsely claim affiliation with StratOps</li><li>Redistribute content in a misleading manner</li><li>Automate abusive collection of platform content</li></ul><p>StratOps reserves the right to restrict or terminate access for violations of these terms.</p><h3>Intellectual Property</h3><p>All StratOps branding, visual design, user interface elements, software components, graphics, logos, documentation, and proprietary content remain the property of BattlespaceX and/or their respective rights holders.</p><p>Nothing within these terms transfers ownership of any intellectual property to users.</p><h3>External Sources &amp; Third-Party Content</h3><p>StratOps may reference, aggregate, summarize, visualize, or display information originating from third-party sources.</p><p>Ownership of such third-party content remains with its respective owners.</p><p>StratOps does not assume responsibility for the accuracy, availability, legality, or continued existence of external information sources.</p><h3>Platform Availability</h3><p>StratOps is provided on an "as available" basis.</p><p>The platform may experience:</p><ul class="wz-list-view"><li>Maintenance periods</li><li>Service interruptions</li><li>Data delays</li><li>Feed outages</li><li>Mapping inaccuracies</li><li>Visualization issues</li><li>Technical failures</li></ul><p>Availability is not guaranteed.</p><h3>Limitation of Liability</h3><p>To the maximum extent permitted by law, BattlespaceX, StratOps, its operators, contributors, partners, and affiliates shall not be liable for:</p><ul class="wz-list-view"><li>Direct damages</li><li>Indirect damages</li><li>Incidental damages</li><li>Consequential damages</li><li>Business interruption</li><li>Financial losses</li><li>Operational decisions</li><li>Security decisions</li><li>Personal or organizational actions taken in reliance upon platform content</li></ul><p>Use of StratOps is entirely at the user's own risk.</p><h3>Access Restriction &amp; Enforcement</h3><p>StratOps reserves the right to suspend, restrict, or permanently revoke access to any user or entity that:</p><ul class="wz-list-view"><li>Violates these Rules of Engagement</li><li>Harms platform operations</li><li>Abuses platform resources</li><li>Engages in unlawful conduct</li><li>Threatens platform security or integrity</li></ul><p>Such actions may occur without prior notice.</p><h3>Modifications</h3><p>These Rules of Engagement may be updated, revised, or replaced at any time.</p><p>Continued use of StratOps following publication of revised terms constitutes acceptance of the updated version.</p><h3>Governing Principles</h3><p>StratOps is designed as an informational situational awareness platform intended to improve understanding of global events through open-source information visualization.</p><p>All information should be independently evaluated and verified before being used for operational, legal, financial, safety, governmental, military, or security-related decisions.</p></div></section><footer><div id="wz-hint" class="wz-hint"><span class="static-icon stratops-ico-assets-alert-1 color-grace-red" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Enter as a guest or <button type="button" id="wz-intro-open-login">Sign In</button> to unlock full capabilities.</span></div><div class="wz-action"><div class="wz-checks"><div class="wz-check" for="intro-disclaimer-check"><input id="intro-disclaimer-check" type="checkbox"/> <span>I understand that StratOps presents OSINT-informed monitoring data and is not an official warning network, or classified intelligence product.</span></div><div class="wz-check-row"><div class="wz-check" for=